    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1210">

                <pb facs="1418" n="1220" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/7–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1210<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary
                            of State to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-29">July 29 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155.…<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1210-f1"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Department has discussed Yugo note (Belgrade’s 296)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1210-f2"/> with British and is now awaiting receipt their views
                    before instructing Embassy Belgrade re reply.</p>
                <pb facs="1419" n="1221" xml:id="pg1221"/>
                <p>We expect that local elections will be held in Venezia Giulia as in other AMG territory at approximately same time such
                    elections are held in other parts of Italy and AMG has already initiated certain preparations to that end.
                    Department however agrees with view set forth in final paragraph Belgrade’s
                        318<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1210-f3"/> that to accept Yugo thesis that area is
                    liberated territory (i. e. Yugo liberated territory) would in effect prejudge
                    final question of sovereignty.</p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1210-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1210-f1-content">
                <p>Here follows a summary of <ref target="#d1207">document No. 1207</ref> and its
                    enclosure.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1210-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1210-f2-content">
                <p>The Embassy’s telegram is not printed. For the text of the Yugoslav note referred
                    to, see the enclosure to <ref target="#d1207">document No. 1207</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1210-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1210-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1209">Document No. 1209</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
